# Forest terrain sketch (replaces the third-party Tileset.png, #189). One char = one pixel; `.` transparent.
# Same 320x112 sheet and tile ids as the old Tileset.png: a piece sits at `at <col> <row>` of the 20x7 sheet.
# The props at tile ids 29 to 137 (`prop-<id>`: the village sign, the bare trees, the ochre tufts) are the third-party sheet's own
# pixels, copied unchanged when the sheet was retired (#189, #236); they are not redrawn yet.
# Walk edge: blade tips on row 0, the straw line on row 1 (the cue), a straw and moss band, dark moss, a shadow line, and
# moss strands hanging over the soil. Soil and rock textures meet seamlessly at every tile edge, so any arrangement works; the
# soil body's 16 px repeat is broken by the body variants of `Block faces` below, which `retile` scatters (D114).
# Unused variants (tile ids no map uses): ground top 1-3, ground body 5-7, ground bottom 9-10, rock fill 12-13 (sheet ids, 0-based).
# The ground piece's left and right columns are the block faces and its bottom row the underside (D114, `Block faces`).
tile 16
# Depth palette (D120, 2026-11-21): the canopy clump u v w is dark leaf green, the props' contour A bark, the sign B D E F H a dark
# wood ramp, the tufts I J K moss (were navy, violet, ochre and teal-moss). The terrain keys are unchanged.
